  "query_preview": "..\nWell Sunday was definitely more active than Saturday\nand this active monsoon pattern is expected to continue to at \nleast Thursday before a drier southwest flow aloft brings a \nsignificant downturn is daily storm activity Friday into next \nweekend.\n\nToday through Thursday will see heightened daily threats for \nstrong to severe thunderstorms, blowing dust, and heavy rain \nleading to flash flooding. The signal surely is leaning toward \ndaily heavy rain chances most of this week with PWATs between \n1.20\" and 1.70\". WPC has placed SE AZ under SLGT chance of \nExcessive Rainfall (ER) today through Thursday. We currently \nhave a flash flood watch in effect for most of the area later \ntoday but may have to think hoisting flash flood watches for \nother days this week especially for areas that are hit. \n\nTemperatures will be near normal levels today and Tuesday, then\nto about 3 to 6 degrees below normal Wednesday and Thursday, \nwith warming thereafter to above normal values for next weekend.",
